{"_id": "25862853|None", "id": "25862853", "infons": {}, "passages": [{"infons": {"journal": "Anticancer Res. 2015 Apr;35(4):2005-8.", "year": "2015", "type": "title", "authors": "Banno E, Togashi Y, Kobayashi Y, Hayashi H, Mitsudomi T, Nishio K"}, "offset": 0, "text": "Afatinib is especially effective against non-small cell lung cancer carrying an EGFR exon 19 deletion.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "3", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000077716", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000077716"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000077716", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "Afatinib", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_Afatinib"}, "text": "Afatinib", "locations": [{"offset": 0, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "4", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "non-small cell lung cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 41, "length": 26}]}, {"id": "5", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 80, "length": 4}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"type": "abstract"}, "offset": 103, "text": "BACKGROUND: A recent pooled analysis of the LUX-LUNG3 and LUX-LUNG6 trials suggested that afatinib (an irreversible epidermal growth factor receptor-tyrosine kinase inhibitor (EGFR-TKI)) is especially effective against non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) carrying an EGFR exon 19 deletion. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Stable viral transfectant HEK293 cell lines carrying an exon 19 deletion (HEK293/19 del) or exon 21 L858R mutation (HEK293/ L858R)) were created and their drug sensitivities to AG1478 (a reversible EGFR-TKI) and afatinib were examined using an MTT assay. Western blot analyses were performed to estimate the phosphorylation of EGFR. RESULTS: In the HEK293/19 del, the 50% inhibitory concentration (IC50) of afatinib was significantly lower than that in the HEK293/ L858R. In addition, afatinib inhibited the phosphorylation of EGFR to a greater degree in the HEK293/19 del than in the HEK293/L858R. CONCLUSION: Our experimental findings suggest that afatinib is especially effective against NSCLC carrying an EGFR exon 19 deletion.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "33", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000077716", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000077716"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000077716", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "Afatinib", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_Afatinib"}, "text": "afatinib", "locations": [{"offset": 193, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "34", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 279, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "35", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "non-small cell lung cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 322, "length": 26}]}, {"id": "36", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "NSCLC", "locations": [{"offset": 350, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "37", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true